exports[`results > of aq_guide read as they did 1`] = `
"rev <epoch>:0
topic ops/property.edit
# property.edit

Set properties of clips and their keyframes, in one step.

Signature: property.edit {timeline, edits:[PropertyEdit]}

Parameters:
- timeline (required): Timeline id (aq_project_status).
- edits (required): Each {"owner":{"clip":id},"path",…,"op"}: "set" a value or keyframes, "clear", "write" at a time, or "setKey", "removeKey", "moveKey", "putKeys", "setInterp".

Returns nothing besides the list of changes.

Errors it can give: not-found, invalid-value, not-animatable, invalid-params, unknown-operation, not-allowed, storage-only, project-locked, read-only, missing-updates, conflict, stale-revision, would-break-document

Examples (illustrative; their ids come from a sample project):
- Fade a property in with two keyframes: {"op":"property.edit","timeline":"main","edits":[{"owner":{"clip":"clip_title"},"path":"opacity","op":"set","value":{"keys":[{"time":"0","value":0},{"time":"1","value":1}]}}]}"
`;

